---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Navbar from "../../components/Navbar.astro";
import Footer from "../../components/Footer.astro";
---

<Layout title="Mapping Supplier Capabilities for Faster Onboarding - Marker">
  <Navbar />
  <main id="main-content">
    <article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 pt-16 pb-16 md:pt-24 md:pb-24">
      <a href="/case-studies" class="mb-8 inline-flex items-center text-sm text-muted-foreground hover:text-foreground">
        <svg class="mr-1 h-4 w-4" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
          <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M15 19l-7-7 7-7"></path>
        </svg>
        All Case Studies
      </a>

      <span class="mb-3 inline-block text-xs font-medium uppercase tracking-wider text-primary">Lifestyle Apparel</span>
      <h1 class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-foreground md:text-3xl">Mapping Supplier Capabilities for Faster Onboarding</h1>

      <div class="mt-8 rounded-lg border border-border bg-muted/50 p-5 text-sm">
        <div class="grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-3">
          <div>
            <span class="block font-medium text-foreground">Company</span>
            <span class="text-muted-foreground">Lifestyle apparel brand with a multi-quarter product-to-market cycle</span>
          </div>
          <div>
            <span class="block font-medium text-foreground">Team</span>
            <span class="text-muted-foreground">Supply chain leadership responsible for vendor management and new supplier qualification</span>
          </div>
          <div>
            <span class="block font-medium text-foreground">Key Challenge</span>
            <span class="text-muted-foreground">No central repository of supplier capabilities; onboarding new vendors required manually mapping the entire process from scratch</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <section class="mt-10">
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-foreground">The Challenge</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">The interim head of supply chain at this lifestyle apparel brand — with 25 years of experience at a major American fashion house — faced a common but under-discussed problem: the company had no central repository of what their suppliers could actually do. Capabilities, certifications, capacity constraints, and specializations lived in the heads of individual team members and in scattered email threads.</p>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">When the team needed to onboard a new supplier — whether to expand capacity, enter a new product category, or respond to country-of-origin changes — the process started nearly from scratch each time. Someone had to manually map out the workflow: what documents the new vendor needed, which approvals were required, what the expected communication cadence should look like, and how the vendor's capabilities aligned with the brand's needs.</p>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">The lack of a capabilities database also meant the team couldn't quickly answer strategic questions: Which of our current suppliers can handle this fabric type? Who has capacity for this production timeline? Which vendors have the certifications required for this market?</p>
      </section>

      <section class="mt-10">
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-foreground">The Approach</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">Marker builds a living supplier capabilities profile from the communication record. As the team works with each vendor — exchanging tech packs, negotiating on materials, discussing production timelines — Marker captures the data points that define what each supplier can do: product categories, fabric capabilities, production volumes, lead times, and certifications mentioned in correspondence.</p>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">For new supplier onboarding, Marker provides a process template derived from how the team has actually worked with similar vendors in the past — not a theoretical checklist, but a real communication-based map of what onboarding looks like in practice. New vendors receive a structured onboarding workflow, and the team can track progress against milestones rather than relying on memory to determine whether all the right steps have been taken.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="mt-10">
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-foreground">Key Takeaways</h2>
        <ul class="mt-3 space-y-2 text-muted-foreground">
          <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
            <span class="mt-1.5 block h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-primary"></span>
            <span>Supplier capabilities profiles built automatically from communication history — product categories, materials, certifications, and capacity</span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
            <span class="mt-1.5 block h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-primary"></span>
            <span>New supplier onboarding guided by templates derived from actual past workflows, not theoretical checklists</span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
            <span class="mt-1.5 block h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-primary"></span>
            <span>Strategic supplier questions answerable on demand: who can handle this fabric, category, or timeline?</span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
            <span class="mt-1.5 block h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-primary"></span>
            <span>Onboarding progress tracked against milestones rather than managed through memory and manual checklists</span>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="mt-12 rounded-lg border border-primary/20 bg-primary/5 p-6 text-center">
        <p class="text-sm font-medium text-foreground">See how Marker helps you build a living database of supplier capabilities.</p>
        <a href="/book-demo" class="mt-4 inline-flex h-10 items-center justify-center rounded-lg bg-primary px-6 text-sm font-medium text-primary-foreground transition-colors hover:bg-primary/90 focus-visible:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-ring focus-visible:ring-offset-2">Book a Demo</a>
      </section>
    </article>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Layout>
